{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485149,"name":"♫果果™","username":"guoxjtu","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/d2c977/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T10:10:28.387Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/2/9/29a73eeebec93b5ea81a14caaef9b99d0a58b921.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/5WtTJ5MP0t87pzLnlCuzDRNgC1r.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/2/9/29a73eeebec93b5ea81a14caaef9b99d0a58b921.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"5WtTJ5MP0t87pzLnlCuzDRNgC1r\" width=\"673\" height=\"287\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e673×287 8.05 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003eOn my Included Usage dashboard, \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-default\u003c/code\u003e is listed under Cursor Models. Does that mean it consumes the Cursor Models monthly quota, or is it only a display grouping while Grok Bot still has its own weekly pool?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-09T07:50:32.568Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":33,"reads":17,"readers_count":16,"score":183.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170875,"topic_slug":"are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate","display_username":"♫果果™","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":128986,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate/170875/1","reactions":[{"id":"heavy_plus_sign","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":487089,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T06:55:50.744Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, good question. Grok Bot usage is separate from your Cursor quota. On Pro, Grok Bot has its own weekly allowance, and the Cursor Models monthly quota is only used by what you do inside the Cursor app. So the percentage you see at the top of Cursor Models is only your Cursor usage, Grok Bot doesn’t take anything from it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-default\u003c/code\u003e line under Cursor Models is a known display issue we’re tracking. The per-model breakdown in Included Usage doesn’t filter out Grok Bot from the per-model rows yet, so it shows up there and looks like it’s taking part of the percentage at the top. This doesn’t affect what you’re actually billed, and it doesn’t affect your remaining Cursor quota. You don’t need to do anything on your account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA couple helpful things to know:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf Grok Bot’s weekly allowance hits 100%, further Grok Bot usage may switch to on-demand if it’s enabled. To prevent that, you can set the on-demand limit to $0.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCloud agents launched by Grok Bot are billed as Cursor usage, because they run in Cursor.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if anything’s still unclear.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-09T06:55:50.744Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":8,"readers_count":7,"score":11.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170875,"topic_slug":"are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate/170875/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":487124,"name":"z l","username":"z_l","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/z/e36b37/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T07:50:18.143Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/deanrie\"\u003e@deanrie\u003c/a\u003e  I can understand what you’re saying that it was a display error and he didn’t actually use up my cursor quota. However, this completely disrupted my usage plan, resulting in my account running out of balance just 11 days before the next reset. I can’t tell anymore. I have to uninstall the bot and never use it again. This lesson is extremely painful.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-09T07:50:30.770Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":16.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170875,"topic_slug":"are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate","display_username":"z l","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132272,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate/170875/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":487290,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T11:25:30.947Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI get that this feels frustrating. It’s hard to plan spending when the breakdown in the dashboard looks confusing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA couple quick notes on how it works, so it’s clearer:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot uses its own separate weekly allowance. The Cursor Models monthly quota is only used by what you do inside Cursor itself. The \u003ccode\u003egrok-bot-default\u003c/code\u003e row under Cursor Models is a display grouping issue we’re tracking. It doesn’t affect your actual Cursor quota usage.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf Grok Bot hits 100% of its weekly allowance, further usage may go to on-demand, if it’s enabled. To prevent that, you can set the on-demand limit to (0). Then usage will stop at the limit and won’t keep going.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot and Cursor reset on different cycles. Grok Bot is weekly. Because of that, seeing something like 11 days until reset can be confusing.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you want someone to check what was charged on your account and why your balance hit zero, email \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e. They can review your specific account details, which isn’t visible from the forum.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if anything still doesn’t add up after that.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-09T11:25:30.947Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170875,"topic_slug":"are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":132272,"username":"z_l","name":"z l","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/z/e36b37/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate/170875/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":487301,"name":"z l","username":"z_l","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/z/e36b37/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T11:52:54.429Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYes, I hope you can do your best to fix it. It would be best to list the bot’s consumption separately and not mix it in with other items. Originally, it was reasonable for them to come from different software divisions. I will clear my name for you. Because I have exhausted all my available funds now, but it can still be confirmed that the bot has its own independent quota. But I have to add one more joke. Your auto credit limit has decreased significantly. I miss the days of unlimited credit. I used pro+ throughout and my total auto credit limit was approximately only 25 billion tokens.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-09T11:52:54.429Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":9,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170875,"topic_slug":"are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate","display_username":"z l","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":132272,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate/170875/10","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":487449,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:06:58.983Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for not dropping the thread. Your point about showing Grok Bot on a separate line makes sense, that’s exactly the kind of display improvement we’re tracking so Grok Bot and Cursor usage don’t look mixed together in Included Usage. I can’t share a timeline yet, but the direction is right, and I passed this along as feedback.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor your balance and the charge details for the current billing cycle, it’s best to email \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e. That team can check your account directly, which we can’t do from the forum.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf anything still doesn’t add up, let me know and we’ll take a look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":11,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-09T14:06:58.983Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":10,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170875,"topic_slug":"are-grok-bot-usage-and-cursor-usage-separate","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read